 "summary": "Yes in both versions. HTTP_PROXY, HTTPS_PROXY and ALL_PROXY were all set to the recording proxy with no NO_PROXY. The product command hook (claude-hook.ps1), synchronous and async, delivered every event over the named pipe; a node command hook delivered every event through its own output file; the proxy captured only the model API requests and the CLI start-up traffic, and none of the markers that only a hook payload carries (hook_event_name, transcript_path, permission_mode, agent-activity, hookEvent, sentAt). The http control run proves the markers would show up if hook data did pass through the proxy.",
 "caveats": [
  "Windows only: the named pipe is a Windows pipe. The bash and zsh wrappers use a different transport (a socket or file) and were not run here; E1 must not enable command-async on POSIX until a CI capture covers them.",
  "Proxy bytes were captured for plain-http traffic and for the bytes sent inside CONNECT tunnels; a TLS tunnel is opaque, but no hook traffic used a tunnel (the proxy log lists the targets)."
 ]
}
